{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments ["<b>And they said to Moses, etc. and we brought near, etc.</b> The meaning of the statement <b>and they said</b>, etc., <b>and not one was missing</b>, etc., is to remove from them any suspicion of stumbling in sin, as is understood from the nature of the offering that they brought — the women's ornaments. And the statement <b>and we brought near</b>, etc., is the reason for the offering, which is to atone for the contemplation of sin, as they said, of blessed memory, in [the tractate] Shabbat (Shabbat 64a), and I explained it in my work (Chefetz Hashem)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The abbreviation חפץ ה׳ is resolved as Chefetz Hashem, a known work by R. Chaim ibn Attar."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:17.282861565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}